# Manufacturing Anomaly Detection

An industrial-grade CNN-based system for detecting manufacturing defects in production lines. This repository implements the architecture that achieved a 23% reduction in manufacturing defect rates across production lines.

## Architecture

![Architecture Diagram](docs/architecture.png)

The system uses a multi-scale CNN architecture with attention mechanisms to identify visual defects across different manufacturing components. It leverages transfer learning from ResNet50 with custom layers designed for industrial manufacturing contexts.

## Key Features
- Multi-scale feature extraction for handling different defect sizes
- Transfer learning approach with fine-tuning for manufacturing domains
- Data augmentation strategies for handling manufacturing variability
- Model explainability for process engineers using feature map visualization
- Production-ready inference pipeline with Docker support

## Results
The model achieves 92.7% accuracy on unseen test data, with precision and recall of 89.3% and 91.2% respectively for defect detection. When deployed in a production environment, it resulted in a 23% reduction in defect rates.

